   "definition_quote": "Let $f$ be a function on the compact domain $D = [0,1]^d$ ... assuming that $\\|f\\|_{k} \\le B$ ... the algorithm selects some $\\xv_t \\in D$, and observes a noisy sample $y_t = f(\\xv_t) + z_t$. Here the noise term is distributed as $N(0,\\sigma^2)$ ... Simple regret: After $T$ rounds, an additional point $\\xv^{(T)}$ is returned, and the simple regret is given by $r(\\xv^{(T)}) = f(\\xv^*) - f(\\xv^{(T)})$."
